  ('privacy_notice', '75ead55502dc1f7bf23fef437d4b1633', 'en', $legal$Privacy Notice (KVKK)$legal$, $legal$DRAFT — Legal review required.

Under Turkish Law No. 6698 on the Protection of Personal Data (KVKK), we, GWAY, as the data controller, process your personal data as follows.

Data processed: email address, username, name, profile and cover images, bio, interests, your posts and interactions on the platform, IP and session logs for security, your phone number for verification, your location for security (country only; your exact location is not stored), your date of birth for the 18+ check, the photos you upload, your messages, and a device token for notifications.

Purposes: creating and managing your account, providing the platform's services, ensuring security, and meeting legal obligations.

Legal grounds: the conclusion and performance of the contract, legal obligation, legitimate interest and, where needed, your explicit consent.

Transfers: Data may be processed on servers abroad belonging to the infrastructure providers we use. Your explicit consent is asked for this transfer.

Your rights: Under Article 11 of the KVKK you have the right to access your data, to ask for it to be corrected or deleted, and to object. You can delete your account from within the app.

Your messages and voice calls: Only the participants of a chat see your private messages. The GWAY team has no tool to view message content, and the team does not review the content of your private messages, including reported ones. The text of a message you report in a group chat is passed to that group's moderators as evidence. Message notifications are delivered through our notification infrastructure provider (Google Firebase) to bring the message's short text to your device; you can turn this off in your notification preferences. Voice calls and live broadcasts are not recorded; who a call was with, when and for how long is stored so that only the two parties can see it. The text and photo of a message you delete are deleted and not kept in an archive; they drop out of technical backups automatically at the end of the backup period. Where there is a legal obligation such as a court order, we may have to share data with the competent authorities to the extent the law requires.$legal$),
  ('distance_sales', 'f15fc6780e8b97261597a14ff0210a12', 'en', $legal$Preliminary Information Form and Distance Sales Agreement$legal$, $legal$DRAFT — Legal review required.

1. Parties
Seller: GWAY (trade name, address, MERSIS number and contact details will be added before launch).
Buyer: The GWAY user who enters the billing details at checkout.

2. Subject
This agreement concerns the use of the GWAY plan the buyer chooses for a group they manage, for the chosen period (monthly or yearly). The plan's name, limits (number of members, events per month, live minutes per month), period, start and estimated end date and total price including taxes are shown on the payment screen.

3. Payment
The price is paid in one go. Payment is taken through PayTR for purchases made from Turkey and through iyzico for purchases made from other countries. Card details are neither seen nor stored by GWAY. There is no automatic renewal; when the period ends, the group returns to the free plan.

4. Performance
The plan is made available electronically and immediately once the payment institution confirms the payment. When moving to a higher plan, the remaining time of the current plan is added to the new plan in proportion to the plan prices. Moving to the same or a lower plan starts at the end of the current period.

5. Right of withdrawal
Under Article 15 of the Distance Contracts Regulation, there is no right of withdrawal for services performed electronically and immediately. The buyer accepts that the plan will be made available upon payment confirmation and that there is therefore no right of withdrawal.

6. Deleting the group and transferring ownership
The plan belongs to the group. When ownership is transferred, the plan stays with the group. If the group is deleted, no refund is made for the remaining time.

7. Personal data
Billing details are processed only to take the payment, to issue invoices and to meet legal record-keeping obligations. Details are in the Privacy Notice (KVKK).

8. Disputes
For disputes, the Consumer Arbitration Committees and Consumer Courts of the buyer's place of residence are competent within the monetary limits announced by the Ministry of Trade.$legal$),
  ('community_rules', 'c494ae740a14c8856062adda6e340811', 'en', $legal$Community Guidelines, Sanctions and Legal Procedures Agreement$legal$, $legal$DRAFT — Legal review required before launch.

This agreement applies to everyone who uses the GWAY app and website (together, the "Platform"). It is read together with the Terms of Use, the Privacy Notice (KVKK) and the Explicit Consent. To use the Platform you must read this text to the end and accept it.

1. DEFINITIONS
- GWAY: The party that operates the Platform and is the data controller of personal data (trade name, address, MERSIS number and contact details will be added before launch).
- User: A natural person who registers on and uses the Platform. Referred to as "you" in this text.
- Group: A community page set up on the Platform. Each group may have an owner, admins, moderators and a disciplinary board.
- Disciplinary Board: Members appointed by the group owner who decide on complaints within the group by voting. If there is no board, the group owner decides.
- Platform Team: The admins and moderators authorized by GWAY.
- Content: Posts, comments, photos, videos, group chats and one-to-one messages, live broadcast conversations and comments, event and poll texts, and profile information.
- Paid Membership: Personal plans (such as the matching plans and Teammate) and the group plans a group owner buys for their group.

2. YOUR RESPONSIBILITY
2.1. You are personally responsible, under civil and criminal law, for all content you share on the Platform, every message you send and every activity you carry out through the Platform.
2.2. GWAY is a hosting provider under Law No. 5651. It is not obliged to check users' content in advance. When it becomes aware of unlawful content, it removes it and applies the sanctions in this agreement.
2.3. You are responsible for any damage that unlawful content or activity causes to third parties or to GWAY. GWAY may claim back from you any amounts it has to pay for this reason.
2.4. Liabilities that cannot be limited by law and your legal rights as a consumer are reserved.

3. PROHIBITED BEHAVIOR
In addition to the app and group rules, the following are prohibited everywhere and under all circumstances. Carrying them out on the Platform or preparing them through the Platform is likewise prohibited:
a) Violence: Using violence against a person or community, calling for, praising or organizing violence.
b) Threats: Threatening a person or their relatives with harm to their life, physical integrity, property or private life (Turkish Penal Code Art. 106).
c) Insult: Words, writings, images or behavior that offend a person's honor, dignity and reputation (TPC Art. 125).
d) Hate and discrimination: Inciting hatred and hostility or discriminating on grounds such as language, race, nationality, color, gender, disability, political opinion, philosophical belief, religion or sect (TPC Arts. 122, 216).
e) Sexual offenses: Sexual harassment, sharing sexual content without consent, and obscenity (TPC Arts. 102, 105, 226). Any content relating to the sexual abuse of children is strictly prohibited and is always reported to the competent authorities (TPC Art. 103).
f) Stalking and private life: Persistently following or disturbing a person, violating the privacy of private life, unlawfully obtaining or spreading personal data (TPC Arts. 123/A, 134, 135, 136).
g) Fraud: Gaining an unfair advantage through fake events, collecting fake fees, impersonation, phishing and similar means (TPC Arts. 157, 158).
h) Drugs and weapons: Trading in narcotic or stimulant substances or encouraging their use (TPC Arts. 188, 190), trading unlicensed weapons and explosives.
i) Terrorism and criminal organizations: Propaganda for a terrorist organization, recruiting members for it or praising it (Law No. 3713 Art. 7), and the activities of criminal organizations.
j) Other offenses: Gambling, illegal betting, infringement of intellectual property and any other activity that is an offense under the legislation in force.
k) Abuse: Spam, fake accounts, accounts in someone else's name, opening a new account to get around a sanction, and trying to bypass the Platform's security measures.

4. COMPLAINT AND REVIEW PROCESS
4.1. Every user can report content or a person they consider to break the rules from within the app. The reported person sees neither the report nor who made it.
4.2. Complaints within a group are first reviewed by the group's moderators. A disciplinary case is opened if needed.
4.3. The group's Disciplinary Board votes on the disciplinary case within 72 hours. Depending on the group setting, a simple majority, two-thirds or unanimity is required. If there is no board, the group owner decides.
4.4. The board decides based on the content within the group: posts, comments, group chat, live broadcast comments and copies of the reported content as it was when reported. The board cannot see your one-to-one (private) messages. Only the Platform Team reviews complaints about private messages.
4.5. In emergencies (for example harassment in a live broadcast), a moderator or board member may mute you for up to 24 hours and remove you from the broadcast. In that case a case is opened automatically.
4.6. Complaints, cases, votes, decisions and sanctions are recorded in a way that cannot be changed.

5. SANCTIONS
5.1. Sanctions that can be applied within a group:
- a warning;
- a mute (1–90 days): you cannot comment or speak in live broadcasts;
- removal from the group;
- a temporary (1–365 days) or permanent ban from the group.
5.2. Sanctions that can be applied across the Platform:
- removal of content;
- suspension of the account during a review;
- temporary (up to 10 years) or permanent closure of the account (ban);
- suspension of the groups you own.
5.3. No one can be sanctioned by someone of equal or lower rank. A group owner cannot be banned in their own group. This rule does not limit the Platform Team's sanctions.
5.4. Opening a new account while your account is closed is prohibited. If detected, the new account is closed for the same period.

6. ILLEGAL ACTIVITY REPORT AND PLATFORM REVIEW
6.1. When the Disciplinary Board finds an illegal activity listed in Article 3, it may propose a ban and mark the case as "illegal activity".
6.2. If the board approves such a case, three things happen at once: you are banned from the group, your account is suspended immediately until the Platform Team reviews it, and the case is sent to the Platform Team with its evidence. You cannot sign in during the suspension.
6.3. The Platform Team reviews the case and the evidence. In the end it either closes your account temporarily or permanently, or clears you and lifts the suspension.
6.4. The board and group admins may use this power only in good faith and based on concrete evidence. The sanctions in this agreement also apply to those who abuse it.

7. COOPERATION WITH LAW ENFORCEMENT AND JUDICIAL AUTHORITIES
7.1. If an activity gives rise to suspicion of a crime, GWAY may share the following with the competent authorities: your account information, your contact details, your IP and access logs, copies of the relevant content, and records of complaints, cases and decisions.
7.2. Authorities that information may be shared with: law enforcement (Police, Gendarmerie), Chief Public Prosecutor's Offices, courts and other competent public bodies.
7.3. Sharing takes place in these cases: where the law provides for it (KVKK Arts. 8/2, 28; Law No. 5651), at the request of the competent authorities, or when there is an urgent danger to a person's life or physical integrity. Cases involving the sexual abuse of children, terrorism and danger to life are reported by the Platform Team on its own initiative.
7.4. Only GWAY makes such reports and transfers data. Group owners, admins and board members cannot transfer your data to anyone. You or any other user always keep the right to file a complaint yourselves.
7.5. Under Law No. 5651 and related legislation, GWAY keeps traffic data (IP address, connection time and similar) for the period set by law.

8. EFFECT ON PAID MEMBERSHIPS
8.1. If your account is closed temporarily or permanently by the Platform Team for breach of this agreement:
- your personal plans (matching plans, Teammate and similar) are cancelled at the moment of closure;
- the groups you own are suspended and their plans are cancelled at the moment of closure;
- no refund is made for the remaining time, and the price paid is not returned.
8.2. When your account is suspended pending review under 6.2, your plans are not cancelled immediately. If your account is closed at the end of the review, 8.1 applies.
8.3. Being banned or removed from a single group only does not affect your paid memberships.
8.4. If the Platform Team clears you or your appeal is accepted, a refund or extension for the unused time cancelled because of the closure will be considered.
8.5. This article applies together with the Distance Sales Agreement. In case of conflict, this article prevails for cases of breach; your statutory consumer rights are reserved.

9. GROUP OWNERS, ADMINS AND BOARD MEMBERS
9.1. Group owners and the admins, moderators and board members they appoint are responsible for the group operating in line with the rules.
9.2. These people use their powers impartially, in good faith and based on evidence. They may not apply sanctions out of personal hostility, discrimination or to exert pressure.
9.3. The group of a group owner who tolerates or organizes illegal activity in their group may be suspended. Articles 5 and 8 also apply to their account.

10. APPEAL
10.1. You can appeal group sanctions from within the app (Settings → My group sanctions) within 7 days of the decision being notified to you. Emergency mutes cannot be appealed.
10.2. Since you cannot sign in when your account is suspended or closed, you can send your appeal by email to the GWAY support address within 30 days. The address will be added before launch. Write your username and the grounds for your appeal in the email.
10.3. The sanction continues while the appeal is reviewed. The result of the appeal is notified to you by email.

11. ACCOUNT DELETION AND DATA RETENTION
11.1. You can always delete your account. However, an illegal activity report made about you, the related evidence and decisions are retained for these purposes: meeting legal obligations, possible judicial proceedings and the establishment, exercise or protection of a right (KVKK Art. 5/2-ç and e). They are retained for the statutory periods and the periods of possible disputes.
11.2. Deleting your account does not remove a sanction already applied or a legal process already started.

12. CHANGES
GWAY may update this agreement. When a new version is published, you will be asked to read and accept the new text to keep using the Platform. Every version you accept is recorded together with the time of acceptance.

13. ACCEPTANCE
When you tick the box and continue, you accept that:
- you have read this agreement to the end and understood it;
- you are responsible for any content and activity that breaks the app and group rules or is illegal;
- in such cases your account may be closed temporarily or permanently with the reason given;
- your paid memberships may be cancelled without a refund;
- where necessary, your information may be shared with law enforcement and judicial authorities.$legal$),
